1. PERSONAL & NON-COMMERCIAL USE
   Free use for individuals, education, research, and personal projects.

2. SMALL COMPANY EXEMPTION
   Companies are exempt from the contribution requirement if they meet ALL:
   - Fewer than 10 employees
   - Annual gross revenue under $1.5 million USD (or equivalent)
   - Not a subsidiary of a larger entity

3. COMMERCIAL USE BY LARGER COMPANIES
   Any company exceeding the above thresholds that uses this Software
   commercially must do BOTH of the following:

   a) COMMUNITY CONTRIBUTION
      Contribute back to the open source community through at least ONE of:
      - Contributing modifications, improvements, or bug fixes to this
        project or related open source projects
      - Sponsoring or donating to open source organizations, foundations,
        or maintainers
      - Open sourcing internal tools, libraries, or utilities used alongside
        this Software
      - Contributing to documentation, tutorials, or educational resources
        that benefit the broader community

      Contributions must be meaningful and ongoing, not one-time gestures.

   b) CHARITABLE GIVING
      Donate an amount equal to at least 1% of gross revenue attributable
      to products or services that use this Software to one or more of:
      - Registered charities (501(c)(3) or equivalent in your jurisdiction)
      - Open source foundations (e.g., OSI, Linux Foundation, Apache Foundation)
      - Social impact programs (education, environment, poverty relief)
      - Community development initiatives

      Existing corporate social responsibility (CSR) or environmental, social,
      and governance (ESG) programs may count toward this requirement if they
      meet the following criteria:
      - The program is publicly documented and independently auditable
      - The donations are made to qualifying organizations as listed above
      - The total annual giving meets or exceeds the 1% threshold

      Payment must be made within 90 days of fiscal year end.

